 /  \/
	Extra utilities!

	There are two extra utilities supplied, which are coded in ARexx:

	AddAddy.rexx	  <- For use withing DirOpus/DiskMaster/MTool
	CompareStrip.rexx <- If you have an previous StripFile you wanna
			     keep, this tool checks which adds that isn't
			     present and adds your new to a file called:
			     S:Lha.Strip.more (You can when manually add them
			     to the original S:Lha.Strip) This is so you
			     won't add adds that are already wildcarded
			     in my strip file like: *.nfo *.displayme and
			     so on..

	How to run them: Just write RX CompareStrip.rexx

	NOTE! Don't take these tools TOO serious.. hehe

	The AddAddy file is usefull if you unpack an archive which you
	have stripped and finds out that there was 2 adds that my stripper
	didn't nuke.. Mark them and choose AddAddy and my program will
	save the adds to the S:Lha.Strip.more file! When you can add
	them to the S:Lha.Strip file and send the Lha.Strip.More to me! :)
	Preferable to Dragons Lair and I will release a new Strip File
	as soon as I get about 20 new adds! The LOGO WAR HAS BEGUN! H0H0

